{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction to this plan's Measured-facts section, recorded rather than silently left standing.\n\nThis plan was certified at `b2dca9bf5eabb122c15637e5e7a4dd858c552362`, where its claim of 6\nin-tree held-out twin modules was true. Gerrit change 3246 (ticket `d52f-823f-894e-499a`,\n\"Retire the _heldout test-module naming convention\") MERGED on 2026-11-02 at 20:03 PDT — minutes\nafter this plan was written. It renamed 5 of those modules to drop the suffix and folded the 6th\ninto its sibling. `git ls-files | grep -c '_heldout'` is now **0**.\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n1. **The \"6 held-out twin modules\" fact is stale.** It was accurate at the reviewed SHA and is\n   not accurate at Gerrit's `main`. The GitHub mirror still reported `b2dca9bf5ea` at the time of\n   this comment, so the attestation's `currency_basis: fail-safe` will mark it stale once the\n   mirror syncs.\n2. **`d278-...`'s remaining scope has lost its referent.** Its 2 halves were seam-guard deletion\n   and held-out twin merging. The seam-guard half never had a referent in the tree —\n   no `*_seam_clean_heldout.py` module has ever existed. The twin-merging half had 6 referents\n   until 3246; it now has 0, and the convention that produced them is retired, so the epic-close\n   automation it proposed would have nothing to act on.\n\nWhat this does NOT establish: that recurrence is impossible. 3246 cleaned the 6 instances but\nadded no guard. Separately, \"held-out\" names a live and correct practice — the held-out RED\noracle in `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md`, which `docs/concurrency.md:970-971`\ndirects to live OUTSIDE the tracked tree, under `$(git rev-parse --git-path heldout)/`. That\npractice is unaffected and must not be confused with the retired in-tree twin convention.\n\nThis epic's child decomposition and its 6th acceptance criterion both need amending to reflect\n`d278`'s obsolescence. Deferred to a single amendment rather than edited piecemeal, because an\nedit now would invalidate the attestation that currently permits work on the claimed children.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793675416795143565,"uuid":"801fc10e-3031-49b2-8def-b3c7a52efa1b"}